window.docContents[229].resolve({"/Baker--Heegner--Stark-route/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Baker--Heegner--Stark-route":{"contents":"\n\nThe long-term route follows the classical Cox-style story around imaginary\nquadratic class-number-one fields, singular moduli, and ring class fields,\nsitting on top of\nthe overall blueprint goal and\nreusing the imaginary Minkowski bound.\nThis is not yet a Lean theorem in the project.\n\nThe route requires substantial CM and\nring-class-field input. The current blueprint records this as an external\nmathematical dependency rather than a completed formalization.\n\nThe Baker--Stark analytic/transcendence ingredients are also external\nassumptions at this stage, complementing\nthe CM/ring-class-field input needed by\nthe Cox-style route.\n\nOnce the external CM and\nanalytic inputs are available, the project\nshould connect them to explicit finite Diophantine checks in quadratic fields.\n\nThe conditional endgame should reuse\nthe existing discriminant,\nsplitting,\nring-of-integers,\nunits, and\nclass-group check layers rather than\nduplicating coordinate arguments.\n\nAll Baker--Heegner--Stark nodes are\ndeliberately marked future or external in this first blueprint. None should be\nread as a completed Lean proof.\n\n","context":"Quadratic Number Fields Blueprint","header":"8. Baker--Heegner--Stark route","id":"/Baker--Heegner--Stark-route/#Quadratic-Number-Fields-Blueprint--Baker--Heegner--Stark-route"}});